The method [cv::ml::SVM::predict](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/db/d7d/classcv_1_1ml_1_1StatModel.html#a1a7e49e1febd10392452727498771bc1) is used to classify an input sample using a trained SVM. In this example we have used this method in order to color the space depending on the prediction done by the SVM. In other words, an image is traversed interpreting its pixels as points of the Cartesian plane. Each of the points is colored depending on the class predicted by the SVM; in dark green if it is the class with label 1 and in dark blue if it is the class with label 2.
