#  Source Code
The following code creates two groups: `Group1` and `SubGroup1`, where `SubGroup1` is a child of `Group1`.
You can download the code from `modules/hdf/samples/create_groups.cpp` of the opencv_contrib source code library.
#include <iostream>
#include <[opencv2/core.hpp](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d0/d9c/core_2include_2opencv2_2core_8hpp.html)>
#include <[opencv2/hdf.hpp](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d7/d55/hdf_8hpp.html)>
using namespace [cv](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d2/d75/namespacecv.html);
int [main](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/dc/d89/highgui__qt_8cpp.html#a0ddf1224851353fc92bfbff6f499fa97)()
{
[Ptr<hdf::HDF5>](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/dc/d84/group__core__basic.html#ga524e5e94ebf48db273a71ab275eaf5b5) h5io = hdf::open("mytest.h5");
// "/" means the root group, which is always present
if (!h5io->hlexists("/Group1"))
h5io->grcreate("/Group1");
else
std::cout << "/Group1 has already been created, skip it.\n";
// Note that Group1 has been created above, otherwise exception will occur
if (!h5io->hlexists("/Group1/SubGroup1"))
h5io->grcreate("/Group1/SubGroup1");
else
std::cout << "/Group1/SubGroup1 has already been created, skip it.\n";
h5io->close();
return 0;
}
#  Explanation
First, we create a HDF5 file
[Ptr<hdf::HDF5>](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/dc/d84/group__core__basic.html#ga524e5e94ebf48db273a71ab275eaf5b5) h5io = hdf::open("mytest.h5");
If the given file does not exist, it will be created. Otherwise, it is open for read and write.
Next, we create the group `Group1`
// "/" means the root group, which is always present
if (!h5io->hlexists("/Group1"))
h5io->grcreate("/Group1");
else
std::cout << "/Group1 has already been created, skip it.\n";
Note that we have to check whether `/Group1` exists or not using the function [cv::hdf::HDF5::hlexists()](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d23/classcv_1_1hdf_1_1HDF5.html#add5b1b96093a2a28994627cd545e3d9e "Check if label exists or not.") before creating it. You can not create a group with an existing name. Otherwise, an error will occur.
Then, we create the subgroup named `Subgroup1`. In order to indicate that it is a sub group of `Group1`, we have to use the group name `/Group1/SubGroup1`:
// Note that Group1 has been created above, otherwise exception will occur
if (!h5io->hlexists("/Group1/SubGroup1"))
h5io->grcreate("/Group1/SubGroup1");
else
std::cout << "/Group1/SubGroup1 has already been created, skip it.\n";
Note that before creating a subgroup, we have to make sure that its parent group exists. Otherwise, an error will occur.
In the end, we have to close the file
h5io->close();
