  * The function that applies the remapping is [cv::remap](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/da/d54/group__imgproc__transform.html#gab75ef31ce5cdfb5c44b6da5f3b908ea4) . We give the following arguments:
    * **src** : Source image
    * **dst** : Destination image of same size as _src_
    * **map_x** : The mapping function in the x direction. It is equivalent to the first component of h(i,j)
    * **map_y** : Same as above, but in y direction. Note that _map_y_ and _map_x_ are both of the same size as _src_
    * **INTER_LINEAR** : The type of interpolation to use for non-integer pixels. This is by default.
    * **BORDER_CONSTANT** : Default
How do we update our mapping matrices _mat_x_ and _mat_y_? Go on reading:
  * **Updating the mapping matrices:** We are going to perform 4 different mappings:
    1. Reduce the picture to half its size and will display it in the middle: 
h(i,j)=(2×i−src.cols/2+0.5,2×j−src.rows/2+0.5)
for all pairs (i,j) such that: src.cols4<i<3⋅src.cols4 and src.rows4<j<3⋅src.rows4
    2. Turn the image upside down: h(i,j)=(i,src.rows−j)
    3. Reflect the image from left to right: h(i,j)=(src.cols−i,j)
    4. Combination of b and c: h(i,j)=(src.cols−i,src.rows−j)


This is expressed in the following snippet. Here, _map_x_ represents the first coordinate of _h(i,j)_ and _map_y_ the second coordinate.
C++
void update_map( int &ind, [Mat](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html) &map_x, [Mat](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html) &map_y )
{
for( int i = 0; i < map_x.[rows](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#abed816466c45234254d25bc59c31245e); i++ )
{
for( int j = 0; j < map_x.[cols](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa3e5a47585c9ef6a0842556739155e3e); j++ )
{
switch( ind )
{
case 0:
if( j > map_x.[cols](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa3e5a47585c9ef6a0842556739155e3e)*0.25 && j < map_x.cols*0.75 && i > map_x.[rows](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#abed816466c45234254d25bc59c31245e)*0.25 && i < map_x.[rows](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#abed816466c45234254d25bc59c31245e)*0.75 )
map_x.[at](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa10d804e90b51d4157b5c26e12c5d2df)<float>(i, j) = 2*( j - map_x.[cols](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa3e5a47585c9ef6a0842556739155e3e)*0.25f ) + 0.5f;
map_y.[at](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa10d804e90b51d4157b5c26e12c5d2df)<float>(i, j) = 2*( i - map_x.[rows](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#abed816466c45234254d25bc59c31245e)*0.25f ) + 0.5f;
else
map_x.[at](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa10d804e90b51d4157b5c26e12c5d2df)<float>(i, j) = 0;
map_y.[at](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa10d804e90b51d4157b5c26e12c5d2df)<float>(i, j) = 0;
break;
case 1:
map_x.[at](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa10d804e90b51d4157b5c26e12c5d2df)<float>(i, j) = (float)j;
map_y.[at](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa10d804e90b51d4157b5c26e12c5d2df)<float>(i, j) = (float)(map_x.[rows](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#abed816466c45234254d25bc59c31245e) - i);
break;
case 2:
map_x.[at](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa10d804e90b51d4157b5c26e12c5d2df)<float>(i, j) = (float)(map_x.[cols](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa3e5a47585c9ef6a0842556739155e3e) - j);
map_y.[at](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa10d804e90b51d4157b5c26e12c5d2df)<float>(i, j) = (float)i;
break;
case 3:
map_x.[at](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa10d804e90b51d4157b5c26e12c5d2df)<float>(i, j) = (float)(map_x.[cols](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa3e5a47585c9ef6a0842556739155e3e) - j);
map_y.[at](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa10d804e90b51d4157b5c26e12c5d2df)<float>(i, j) = (float)(map_x.[rows](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#abed816466c45234254d25bc59c31245e) - i);
break;
default:
break;
} // end of switch
}
}
ind = (ind+1) % 4;
}
