}
equalizeHist( gray, gray );
face_cascade.detectMultiScale( gray, faces, 1.1, 3,0, Size(30, 30) );
After doing some preprocessing, we first have to detect possible face regions (which will be stored in a `vector<Rect>`. Also, the image is resized to a smaller size as processing speed is faster with small images.
