#  Introduction
In this tutorial, we will introduce the APIs for TextRecognitionModel and TextDetectionModel in detail.
##  TextRecognitionModel
In the current version, [cv::dnn::TextRecognitionModel](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/de/dee/classcv_1_1dnn_1_1TextRecognitionModel.html) only supports CNN+RNN+CTC based algorithms, and the greedy decoding method for CTC is provided. For more information, please refer to the 
Before recognition, you should `setVocabulary` and `setDecodeType`.
  * "CTC-greedy", the output of the text recognition model should be a probability matrix. The shape should be `(T, B, Dim)`, where
    * `T` is the sequence length
    * `B` is the batch size (only support `B=1` in inference)
    * and `Dim` is the length of vocabulary +1('Blank' of CTC is at the index=0 of Dim).
  * "CTC-prefix-beam-search", the output of the text recognition model should be a probability matrix same with "CTC-greedy".
    * The algorithm is proposed at Hannun's 
    * `setDecodeOptsCTCPrefixBeamSearch` could be used to control the beam size in search step.
    * To further optimize for big vocabulary, a new option `vocPruneSize` is introduced to avoid iterate the whole vocbulary but only the number of `vocPruneSize` tokens with top probability.


[cv::dnn::TextRecognitionModel::recognize()](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/de/dee/classcv_1_1dnn_1_1TextRecognitionModel.html#ad8bfaa53724392dc9477fb55168a0340) is the main function for text recognition.
  * The input image should be a cropped text image or an image with `roiRects`
  * Other decoding methods may supported in the future


##  TextDetectionModel
[cv::dnn::TextDetectionModel](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d4/de1/classcv_1_1dnn_1_1TextDetectionModel.html) API provides these methods for text detection:
  * [cv::dnn::TextDetectionModel::detect()](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d4/de1/classcv_1_1dnn_1_1TextDetectionModel.html#a057582352eac7422cf1a47a7e3e463a7 "Performs detection.") returns the results in std::vector<std::vector<Point>> (4-points quadrangles)
  * [cv::dnn::TextDetectionModel::detectTextRectangles()](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d4/de1/classcv_1_1dnn_1_1TextDetectionModel.html#aa85568c1a42dbed91e95c3b7370ee76c "Performs detection.") returns the results in std::vector<cv::RotatedRect> (RBOX-like)


In the current version, [cv::dnn::TextDetectionModel](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d4/de1/classcv_1_1dnn_1_1TextDetectionModel.html) supports these algorithms:
  * use [cv::dnn::TextDetectionModel_DB](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/db/d0f/classcv_1_1dnn_1_1TextDetectionModel__DB.html) with "DB" models
  * and use [cv::dnn::TextDetectionModel_EAST](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d8/ddc/classcv_1_1dnn_1_1TextDetectionModel__EAST.html) with "EAST" models


The following provided pretrained models are variants of DB (w/o deformable convolution), and the performance can be referred to the Table.1 in the [paper](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/\(https:/arxiv.org/abs/1911.08947\)). For more information, please refer to the 
You can train your own model with more data, and convert it into ONNX format. We encourage you to add new algorithms to these APIs.
