#  Goal
In this tutorial you will learn:
  * what is _linear blending_ and why it is useful;
  * how to add two images using **addWeighted()**


#  Theory 

Note
    The explanation below belongs to the book 
From our previous tutorial, we know already a bit of _Pixel operators_. An interesting dyadic (two-input) operator is the _linear blend operator_ :
g(x)=(1−α)f0(x)+αf1(x)
By varying from 0→1 this operator can be used to perform a temporal _cross-dissolve_ between two images or videos, as seen in slide shows and film productions (cool, eh?)
