Closing the video is automatic when the objects destructor is called. However, if you want to close it before this you need to call its [cv::VideoCapture::release](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d8/dfe/classcv_1_1VideoCapture.html#afb4ab689e553ba2c8f0fec41b9344ae6) function. The frames of the video are just simple images. Therefore, we just need to extract them from the [cv::VideoCapture](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d8/dfe/classcv_1_1VideoCapture.html) object and put them inside a _Mat_ one. The video streams are sequential. You may get the frames one after another by the [cv::VideoCapture::read](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d8/dfe/classcv_1_1VideoCapture.html#a473055e77dd7faa4d26d686226b292c1) or the overloaded >> operator: 
